{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Behold, I am of uncircumcised lips, and how will Pharaoh hear me.</b> Above, when the command of the Holy One, blessed be He, came to both of them, Moses was silent, for he thought the speech would come to Aaron. And now, when He returned and said to him alone ״all that I speak to you,״ he returned to raise again the argument of uncircumcised lips that he had already mentioned, saying ״Behold, I am of uncircumcised lips,״ that is to say: I am not worthy to speak to the people, much less to the king. And the Holy One, blessed be He, answered him."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:35.864193828Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}